            "lower_row_ss": [
                [
                    "",
                    "",
                    "qualification of the merger as a reorganization under Section 368(a)(1)(A) of the Code, (ii) the tax consequences of the Domestication under Sections 367(b) and 368(a)(1)(F) of the Code, (iii) the treatment of the PIPE shares, including the absence of Section 351 or Section 368 treatment for the PIPE, (iv) the tax treatment of the Earnout Shares, including the application of the installment sale rules and the open transaction doctrine, and (v) the tax treatment of the warrants (both private placement and public warrants) in connection with the Domestication and the merger. The memorandum concludes that the merger should qualify as a reorganization under Section 368(a)(1)(A) and that the Domestication should qualify as a reorganization under Section 368(a)(1)(F) of the Code."
